            <ArticleTitle>Common Foot and Ankle Injuries: What Not to Miss and How Best to Manage.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>98-104</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7556/jaoa.2017.020</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Injuries to the foot and ankle are commonly encountered, especially among athletes, and can lead to morbidity if not managed appropriately. Health care professionals must have a firm understanding of injury anatomy, diagnoses, and management. This article provides a review of lateral talus process fractures, os trigonum injuries, Lisfranc injuries, turf toe, navicular stress fractures, and syndesmotic injuries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
